        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಮನವೊಲಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮನವೊಲಿಸು — manavolisu — \"to persuade\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಮ್ಮನನ್ನು ಮನವೊಲಿಸಲು ನನಗೆ ಒಂದು ವಾರ ಬೇಕಾಯಿತು. ammanannu manavolisalu nanage ondu vāra bēkāyitu. It took me a week to persuade Mother."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಮನವೊಲಿಸಿದೆ, manavoliside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The person persuaded takes -ಅನ್ನು."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮನವೊಲಿಸು (manavolisu) is built from two parts: mana, \"mind\" (Sanskrit manas, CDIAL 9822), and olisu, \"to win over\", from native ol / oli, \"to be pleased, to favour\" (DEDR 1006)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
