            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪ್ರೇರೇಪಿಸು — prērēpisu — \"to motivate; to urge\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಶಿಕ್ಷಕಿ ನನ್ನನ್ನು ಓದಲು ಪ್ರೇರೇಪಿಸಿದರು. śikṣaki nannannu ōdalu prērēpisidaru. The teacher motivated me to study."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಪ್ರೇರೇಪಿಸಿದೆ, prērēpiside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The person urged takes -ಅನ್ನು, the aim the -ಅಲು form: ಓದಲು, to study."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪ್ರೇರೇಪಿಸು (prērēpisu) is usually traced to Sanskrit preraṇa, \"setting in motion, urging, inciting\" (Monier-Williams), from pra-īr, \"to urge on\", with the Kannada verb ending -isu; how the shape -ēpisu arose is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
